  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66458,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 15,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mucinous cystadenomas involve the periphery of the lung.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:51:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66459,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 15,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesions are usually found incidentally in asymptomatic patients.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:51:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66460,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 15,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mucinous cystadenoma is exceedingly rare. There is mild female predominance, and most patients are in their sixth or seventh decade of life.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:51:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66461,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 15,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No predisposing factors are known.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:51:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66462,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 15,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:51:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66463,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 15,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "<p>The lesion consists of a localized mucin-filled cyst not associated with an airway. The tumour size ranges from &lt;&nbsp;10 to 70 mm. The cyst wall is thin and lacks mural nodules.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-02T10:40:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66464,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 15,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour consists of a localized cyst filled with mucin, which may be surrounded by a fibrous wall {15923171}. The lining of the cyst wall consists of a discontinuous single layer of low-cuboidal to tall columnar mucin-secreting epithelium. Nuclear atypia is absent or at most mild, and mitoses are absent or rare {1699507; 20549459}. Mild papillary folding may be present {1699507; 8635055}, but micropapillary fronds, necrosis, overt cytological atypia, or invasive growth is absent. Extravasated acellular mucin may be associated with foreign body giant cell reaction and chronic inflammation {15269012; 1699507}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>The lining cells are positive for pancytokeratin and are rarely positive for CEA {1699507}. TTF1 and surfactant protein are usually negative {20549459; 1699507}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The primary entity in the differential diagnosis is colloid carcinoma of the lung, which includes what was previously known as mucinous cystadenocarcinoma. The spread of the tumour beyond the wall of the cyst in either a lepidic or an invasive fashion, significant cytological atypia, and necrosis are indicators of malignancy {1863181; 8635055; 15923171}. Thorough sampling is necessary, because malignant histology may be only focally present within a tumour that otherwise appears benign {15923171}. Metastatic carcinoma from the gastrointestinal tract or ovary should be excluded by extensive workup. Developmental and postinfectious bronchogenic cysts may also be a consideration. They usually show coexistent ciliated cells, in contrast to mucinous cystadenoma. A subset of mucinous cystic neoplasms harbouring borderline histology with regard to nuclear and architectural atypia has been described, although there is no consensus on diagnostic criteria, and cases have been reported to behave in a benign fashion {2001880; 15923171}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:51:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66465,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 15,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FNA specimens may contain mucin and/or goblet cells, but a diagnosis requires surgical excision.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:51:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66466,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 15,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Genetic abnormalities have not been reported.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T10:51:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66467,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 15,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Circumscribed mucin-filled lung cyst surrounded by mucinous cells</li>\r\n<li>Overt cytological atypia and invasion are absent</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-04T09:58:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
